Build the default log file names with the platform's path delimiter.

The session log's and the XML log's defaults are written as literals,
%TEMP%\!S.log and %TEMP%\!S.xml. On POSIX the backslash is not a path
delimiter, so the log was created beside the temporary directory, named
"tmp\!S.log", instead of in it. Built with IncludeTrailingBackslash, as the
random seed file's default already is, the delimiter is the platform's:
on Windows the same backslash as before, so upstream's behaviour is
unchanged. Line counts are unchanged.

--- a/source/core/Configuration.cpp
+++ b/source/core/Configuration.cpp
@@ -264,1 +264,1 @@
-  FActionsLogFileName = L"%TEMP%\\!S.xml";
+  FActionsLogFileName = IncludeTrailingBackslash(L"%TEMP%") + L"!S.xml";
@@ -2252,1 +2252,1 @@
-  return L"%TEMP%\\!S.log";
+  return IncludeTrailingBackslash(L"%TEMP%") + L"!S.log";
